{
    "background_story": "Cherry was a rare and beautiful wood duck who lived in a serene wetland. She was a member of the anseriformes family, characterized by her broad, flat beak and vibrant plumage. Cherry loved to explore the winding waterways, discovering hidden treasures like aquatic plants and shiny pebbles. Her feathers glistened in shades of green, purple, and gold, making her a stunning sight to behold. As the seasons changed, Cherry would migrate with her flock to warmer climates, always returning to her beloved wetland in the spring. She was a gentle soul, often taking young ducklings under her wing and teaching them the ways of the water. Cherry's beauty and kindness made her a cherished member of the wetland community, and her anseriformes heritage was a source of pride for her and her fellow ducks.",
